ffmpeg: in the ARM64EC yuv2rgb NEON code, narrow the blue sums before other outputs overwrite them.

Wine's ARM64EC port of swscale's yuv2rgb_neon.S keeps its sums in v10 to v15 (v16 to v31 are not available to
ARM64EC code), and several output layouts use v10 and v11 as destinations: bgra writes R2 to v10 before B1 is read
from it, argb and abgr write G2 to v10, gbrp writes R1 and R2 to v10 and v11. The blue of half of every 16 pixels
came out wrong, so YUV video converted to BGRA (Media Foundation's video processor, msvproc, for an x86-64 program on
the arm64 engine) showed vertical stripes every 16 pixels and wrong colours. The two blue sums are now narrowed
first. rgba and rgb24 were already right and are unchanged in effect.

Checked on an M4: the first frame of a 3840x2160 H.264 video through the source reader with video processing to
RGB32 matches FFmpeg's C path (av_force_cpu_flags(0)) within 2 on every sampled byte and no pixel differs by more
than 16, where before the image was striped and tinted. Upstream Wine master (11.19) has the same code.

diff -ruN a/libs/ffmpeg/libswscale/arm64ec/yuv2rgb_neon.S b/libs/ffmpeg/libswscale/arm64ec/yuv2rgb_neon.S
--- a/libs/ffmpeg/libswscale/arm64ec/yuv2rgb_neon.S	2026-10-12 23:18:44
+++ b/libs/ffmpeg/libswscale/arm64ec/yuv2rgb_neon.S	2026-10-12 23:18:44
@@ -202,12 +202,15 @@
         add             v15.8h, v5.8h, v15.8h                           // Y2 + G2
         add             v10.8h, v4.8h, v10.8h                           // Y1 + B1
         add             v11.8h, v5.8h, v11.8h                           // Y2 + B2
+        // The blue sums live in v10 and v11, which several output layouts also use as destinations
+        // (bgra writes R2 to v10, argb writes G2 to v10, gbrp writes R1/R2 to v10/v11): narrow them
+        // first, before any other output can overwrite them.
+        sqrshrun        \b1, v10.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y1 + B1) >> 1)
+        sqrshrun        \b2, v11.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y2 + B1) >> 1)
         sqrshrun        \r1, v12.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y1 + R1) >> 1)
         sqrshrun        \r2, v13.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y2 + R1) >> 1)
         sqrshrun        \g1, v14.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y1 + G1) >> 1)
         sqrshrun        \g2, v15.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y2 + G1) >> 1)
-        sqrshrun        \b1, v10.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y1 + B1) >> 1)
-        sqrshrun        \b2, v11.8h, #1                                 // clip_u8((Y2 + B1) >> 1)
 .endm
 
 .macro declare_func ifmt ofmt
